Genie V2 — the legacy discovery engine
======================================

This directory holds the second-generation agent. It is NOT deprecated and it
is NOT dead code. It is the engine that:

  * the deployed Genie web app (`genie/`, Vercel + Render) still runs against,
  * 111 scripts in `scripts/` still import,
  * produced every portal currently delivered to the customer, and
  * still owns the only working T&C waterfall — 3,114 rows on the August4000
    sheet are waiting on it.

It was moved here on 2026-08-31 for one reason: readability. V3 is ~3,500 lines
and was buried under ~15,800 lines of V2 in a flat `agent/` directory. Nothing
about how it runs changed.


-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. EVERY OLD IMPORT PATH STILL WORKS
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

    import agent.magic                  ->  agent.legacy.magic
    from agent.pipeline import ...      ->  agent.legacy.pipeline
    from agent.stages.discovery import  ->  agent.legacy.stages.discovery
    from agent.stages.js_renderer ...   ->  agent.legacy.stages.js_renderer

You do not need to update anything. Shims left at the original paths rebind
`sys.modules[__name__]` to the real module object, so:

    agent.magic is agent.legacy.magic   ->  True

That aliasing is deliberate and load-bearing. A shim that merely RE-EXPORTED
names would create a SECOND module object, and the module-level caches, locks
and `_PARENT_PORTAL_CACHE`-style state inside the V2 engine would silently
diverge between the two copies — a bug that only appears under concurrency and
looks like random cache misses.

`agent/stages/` needs only a package-level shim: once `sys.modules['agent.stages']`
is the legacy package, submodule imports resolve through its `__path__`.


-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2. RUNNING IT
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

All entry points verified working on 2026-08-31.

    # one organisation, full pipeline
    .venv/bin/python scripts/run_single.py --help

    # next N organisations
    .venv/bin/python scripts/run_batch.py --help

    # discovery only (no T&C)
    .venv/bin/python scripts/run_batch_discovery.py --help

    # T&C analysis only
    .venv/bin/python scripts/run_batch_tnc_analysis.py --help

    # office sheet: fill portals in place, per state tab
    .venv/bin/python scripts/run_portal_sheet.py --help

Or call the engine directly:

    from dotenv import load_dotenv; load_dotenv(".env")
    import agent.magic as M
    portals = M.discover("Bangladesh University of Engineering & Technology",
                         "buet.ac.bd", "Bangladesh")
    # -> [{'url': 'https://biis.buet.ac.bd/BIIS_WEB/Login.do',
    #      'category': 'Student Portal', ...}, ...]

Long batch runs use the daemonised + sharded pattern; see the main README
section "Running batches" for the driver shape and the rules that make it
survive overnight.


-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
3. WHAT IS IN HERE
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

    magic.py           1,178  condensed discovery entry point (harvest ->
                              fetch -> LLM judge -> filters). What the batch
                              runners actually call.
    magic_tnc.py         365  inline T&C attach used by magic.discover()
    pipeline.py          185  stage sequencing for the full pipeline
    orchestrator.py      114  top-level run loop
    stages/           13,967  the engine proper:
      discovery.py      5,031   rule-based discovery
      discovery_rules.py 3,600  recognition rules, shortname/geography logic
      tc_finder.py      2,378   T&C search
      tc_levels.py      1,315   the level cascade (portal host -> linked
                                university -> parent domain -> vendor)
      tc_analyzer.py      925   renders a T&C page, returns a
                                Yes/Maybe/No scraping-permission verdict
      js_renderer.py      368   Playwright/Chromium rendering
      sheet_writer.py     162   writes results back to Sheets
      discovery_claude.py 164   Claude fallback for hard rows
      confidence.py        19

Modules that stayed in `agent/` because BOTH generations use them:
`config.py` (the 90 shared-platform patterns live here), `sheets_client.py`,
`state.py`, `proxy.py`, `regions.py`, `anthropic_client.py`.


-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
4. THINGS THAT WILL BITE YOU
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

THE PROXY FAILS CLOSED. If Bright Data rejects our IP
(`401 ip_blacklisted`), every proxied fetch returns status 0 and the reviewer
writes "unreachable (status 0) — remove" for portals that are perfectly alive.
This has produced dozens of false removals. ALWAYS probe first:

    .venv/bin/python -c "
    from dotenv import load_dotenv; load_dotenv('.env')
    import requests, agent.magic as M
    print(requests.get('https://api.ipify.org',
          proxies=M._proxies('https://x.edu.br/'), timeout=25).text)"
    # expect a FOREIGN exit IP, not a 401

"UNREACHABLE" USUALLY MEANS SLOW, NOT DEAD. Re-checking 52 "unreachable"
portals at a longer timeout flipped 26 of them to working. University servers
in Nigeria, Bangladesh and Indonesia routinely take 8-15s for a first byte.

WEB SEARCH IS OFF. `MAGIC_WEB_SEARCH=0` by default: DuckDuckGo rate-limits the
scraper to zero results while still costing ~72s per org across 6 sequential
queries. It was the single biggest harvest cost. V3 hit the identical wall —
129 errors against 2 successes under batch load.

THE OAUTH TOKEN EXPIRES EVERY 7 DAYS while the consent screen is in Testing,
and long unattended runs die mid-batch when it does. Publish the consent
screen to production, or re-auth interactively from a terminal you can watch.

RESOLVE SHEET COLUMNS BY HEADER, NEVER BY LETTER. The Portals TnC layout has
changed several times; letter-indexed writers silently put verdicts in the
`Category` column.


-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
5. WHEN THIS DIRECTORY CAN BE DELETED
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Not yet. In order:

  1. V3 reaches parity on portal recall (it is at 40.1% ground-truth host match
     against V2's delivered results; see the main README).
  2. `genie/` is repointed off `agent.config` / `agent.sheets_client` /
     `agent.stages.js_renderer` / `agent.pipeline`.
  3. The outstanding T&C pass on the August4000 sheet is finished.
  4. `scripts/_build_agent_kb.py` stops reading the platform table from
     `agent/config.py`.

Only then is this ~15,800 lines safe to remove, in one clean commit.
